{"title":"1986 CMO Problems","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Problems\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problems</span></a>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-2 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Problem_1\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1.1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 1</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-2 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Problem_2\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1.2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 2</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-2 tocsection-4\"><a href=\"#Problem_3\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1.3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 3</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-2 tocsection-5\"><a href=\"#Problem_4\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1.4</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 4</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-2 tocsection-6\"><a href=\"#Problem_5\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1.5</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 5</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-2 tocsection-7\"><a href=\"#Problem_6\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1.6</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 6</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-8\"><a href=\"#See_Also\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">See Also</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problems\">Problems</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1986_CMO_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problems\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_1\">Problem 1</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1986_CMO_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h3>\n<p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/0/4/e047bc14560bc613b17fb1ba735bba221764510a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_1, a_2, \\cdots, a_n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"103\" height=\"11\" /> be real numbers. If the sum of any two of them is non-negative, then for any non-negative real numbers <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/f/a/2fa7c5d7fe934004ef357be4f3be8e33d85543a7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x_1, x_2, \\cdots x_n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"97\" height=\"13\" /> satisfying\n\\begin{equation}\nx_1 + x_2 + \\cdots + x_n = 1,\n\\end{equation}\nthe inequality\n\\begin{equation}\na_1 x_1 + a_2 x_2 + \\cdots + a_n x_n \\ge a_1 x_1^2 + a_2 x_2^2 + \\cdots + a_n x_n^2\n\\end{equation}\nholds. Prove the proposition above as well as its converse.\n</p>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_2\">Problem 2</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1986_CMO_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 2\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h3>\n<p>In triangle <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/2/a/e2a559986ed5a0ffc5654bd367c29dfc92913c36.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$ABC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"44\" height=\"14\" />, the altitude <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/c/5/bc56862b1fdb71204894da278e42ef75de73a40b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AD$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"31\" height=\"14\" /> on side <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/c/5/6c52a41dcbd739f1d026c5d4f181438b75b76976.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$BC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"31\" height=\"14\" /> is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/d/f/edf074831eb5bc9e61d6d6e09f525a86e3068f6a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$12$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" />, and the angle bisector <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/a/6/9a65c05bd85d2609bea5db2b109ed5f556463511.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AE$\" width=\"27\" height=\"13\" /> of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/b/1/7b1ac662f7ddbbce489953c8b7693848239564aa.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\angle A$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"28\" height=\"14\" /> has a length of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/3/0/030e19e4e2f1c074127cb50581e8496470c5419f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$13$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" />. Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/e/4/2e4f923da2498343a5b6f32731114d6dda6603d9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AF = m$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"70\" height=\"14\" /> be the median on side <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/c/5/6c52a41dcbd739f1d026c5d4f181438b75b76976.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$BC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"31\" height=\"14\" />. Find the range of values of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/5/0/f5047d1e0cbb50ec208923a22cd517c55100fa7b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"18\" height=\"10\" /> for which <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/b/1/7b1ac662f7ddbbce489953c8b7693848239564aa.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\angle A$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"28\" height=\"14\" /> is acute, right, and obtuse, respectively.\n</p>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_3\">Problem 3</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1986_CMO_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=4\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 3\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h3>\n<p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/7/4/a74abffff135a2b2028cf2d2eeaac472825a0e3e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$z_1, z_2, \\cdots z_n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"92\" height=\"13\" /> be complex numbers satisfying <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/e/2/fe23c66de3efc033fb05ed34b160b15b2041c52f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\lvert z_1 \\rvert + \\lvert z_2 \\rvert + \\cdots + \\lvert z_n \\rvert = 1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"203\" height=\"20\" />. Prove that among these <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" /> complex numbers, there must exist some of them such that the modulus of their sum is at least <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/3/b/43ba19be0e30b99142416ebfbe17670437c8453e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{1}{6}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"15\" height=\"38\" />.\n</p>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_4\">Problem 4</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1986_CMO_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=5\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 4\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h3>\n<p>The four vertices of quadrilateral <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/0/8/808ca848ecfdc79b2111c12667d66469be788d19.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P_1 P_2 P_3 P_4$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"78\" height=\"17\" /> lie on the sides of triangle <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/2/a/e2a559986ed5a0ffc5654bd367c29dfc92913c36.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$ABC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"44\" height=\"14\" />. Prove that among the four triangles <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/d/e/fdeff84fbb19b5242c39fffe43cad6923be0398e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P_1 P_2 P_3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"55\" height=\"15\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/b/0/3b0d2c4e74776041b10d6b691d966f595a7f5955.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P_1 P_2 P_4$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"59\" height=\"17\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/6/d/96d479764070bc5cf361474be80455a0c0117f53.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P_1 P_3 P_4$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"59\" height=\"17\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/3/e/c3e6d153bdffa0b662df1c12478cc061a2e77754.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P_2 P_3 P_4$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"59\" height=\"17\" />, at least one has an area not greater than one-fourth of the area of triangle <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/2/a/e2a559986ed5a0ffc5654bd367c29dfc92913c36.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$ABC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"44\" height=\"14\" />.\n</p>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_5\">Problem 5</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1986_CMO_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=6\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 5\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h3>\n<p>Is it possible to arrange the numbers <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/6/416c073cf023c39218b02d41c42c7eb53649691b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1, 1, 2, 2, \\cdots, 1986, 1986$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"187\" height=\"17\" /> in a line such that there is exactly <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/e/dce34f4dfb2406144304ad0d6106c5382ddd1446.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> number between the two <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/e/dce34f4dfb2406144304ad0d6106c5382ddd1446.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />s, exactly <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/c/41c544263a265ff15498ee45f7392c5f86c6d151.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> numbers between the two <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/c/41c544263a265ff15498ee45f7392c5f86c6d151.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />s, ..., exactly <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/d/2/9d2aea70a9495d66d81a8dcbdcb9dfd80923af93.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1986$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"35\" height=\"13\" /> numbers between the two <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/d/2/9d2aea70a9495d66d81a8dcbdcb9dfd80923af93.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1986$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"35\" height=\"13\" />s? Prove your conclusion.\n</p>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_6\">Problem 6</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1986_CMO_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=7\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 6\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h3>\n<p>Color every point in the plan either black or white, in an arbitrary manner. Prove that there must exist an equilateral triangle with side length <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/e/dce34f4dfb2406144304ad0d6106c5382ddd1446.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> or <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/c/7/6c77cf4b63af80bfbc6a9ad9b4b9e8e549e77d78.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\sqrt{3}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"24\" height=\"18\" /> whose three vertices are of the same color.\n</p><p><br />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_Also\">See Also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1986_CMO_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=8\" title=\"Edit section: See Also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:40%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1986_CMO(CHINA)\" title=\"1986 CMO(CHINA)\">1986 CMO(CHINA)</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1986_CMO(CHINA)_Problems\" title=\"1986 CMO(CHINA) Problems\">Problems</a></b> • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"http://www.artofproblemsolving.com/Forum/resources.php?c=182&amp;cid=27&amp;year=1986\">Resources</a>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b>--</b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1987_CMO(CHINA)\" title=\"1987 CMO(CHINA)\">1987 CMO(CHINA)</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"3\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1986_CMO(CHINA)_Problems/Problem_1\" title=\"1986 CMO(CHINA) Problems/Problem 1\">1</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1986_CMO(CHINA)_Problems/Problem_2\" title=\"1986 CMO(CHINA) Problems/Problem 2\">2</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1986_CMO(CHINA)_Problems/Problem_3\" title=\"1986 CMO(CHINA) Problems/Problem 3\">3</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1986_CMO(CHINA)_Problems/Problem_4\" title=\"1986 CMO(CHINA) Problems/Problem 4\">4</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1986_CMO(CHINA)_Problems/Problem_5\" title=\"1986 CMO(CHINA) Problems/Problem 5\">5</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1986_CMO(CHINA)_Problems/Problem_6\" title=\"1986 CMO(CHINA) Problems/Problem 6\">6</a>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"3\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=CMO(CHINA)_Problems_and_Solutions\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"CMO(CHINA) Problems and Solutions\"> All CMO(CHINA) Problems and Solutions</a></b>\n</td></tr></tbody></table>\n<!-- \nNewPP limit report\nCached time: 20261018043127\nCache expiry: 86400\nReduced expiry: false\nComplications: [show‐toc]\nCPU time usage: 0.027 seconds\nReal time usage: 0.043 seconds\nPreprocessor visited node count: 211/1000000\nPost‐expand include size: 963/2097152 bytes\nTemplate argument size: 57/2097152 bytes\nHighest expansion depth: 3/100\nExpensive parser function count: 0/100\nUnstrip recursion depth: 0/20\nUnstrip post‐expand size: 5881/5000000 bytes\n-->\n<!--\nTransclusion expansion time report (%,ms,calls,template)\n100.00%    7.703      1 Template:CMO_box\n100.00%    7.703      1 -total\n-->\n\n<!-- Saved in parser cache with key wiki-wiki_:pcache:37968:|#|:idhash:canonical and timestamp 20261018043127 and revision id 293191. Rendering was triggered because: api-parse\n -->\n</div>"}